.DS_Store
*.log

# All of these hold real secrets or personal data once the site is live
# (admin/technician passwords, MSG91 API keys, real customer bookings,
# phone numbers) — none of it belongs in git history, which is permanent
# and hard to fully scrub even after deleting a file. Matching .example
# files are committed instead with placeholder values — after cloning,
# copy each one to its real name (e.g. data/admin.json.example →
# data/admin.json) and fill in your real values there.
data/admin.json
data/sub-admins.json
data/technicians.json
data/customers.json
data/bookings.json
data/referrals.json
data/referral-uses.json
data/verified-phones.json
data/technician-applications.json
data/otp-config.json
data/notification-config.json
data/sessions/
public/uploads/

# Holds the real Together.ai API key (and any other real secrets) once
# filled in — must never be committed. .env.example (with placeholder
# values) is committed instead; copy it to .env and fill in your real
# key after cloning.
.env
